From: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: say why GDM3/GDM4 QoS is refused on a WAN port

Distinguish an already-configured WAN QoS qdisc from GDM2 carrying the WAN
role in airoha_enable_qos_for_gdm34() extack messages, because GDM3/GDM4 HW
QoS structurally requires GDM2 loopback and cannot coexist with WAN on GDM2.

Origin: archive/xr1710g-v1@e85677d284c0
Signed-off-by: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -3614,10 +3614,16 @@ static int airoha_enable_qos_for_gdm34(s
 
 	wan_dev = airoha_get_wan_gdm_dev(eth);
 	if (wan_dev) {
-		if (test_bit(AIROHA_DEV_F_TX_QOS, &wan_dev->flags) ||
-		    wan_dev->port->id == AIROHA_GDM2_IDX) {
+		if (test_bit(AIROHA_DEV_F_TX_QOS, &wan_dev->flags)) {
 			NL_SET_ERR_MSG_MOD(extack,
-					   "QoS configured for WAN device");
+					   "QoS already configured for WAN device");
+			err = -EBUSY;
+			goto error_unlock;
+		}
+
+		if (wan_dev->port->id == AIROHA_GDM2_IDX) {
+			NL_SET_ERR_MSG_MOD(extack,
+					   "GDM2 carries the WAN port and is needed for the GDM3/GDM4 QoS loopback");
 			err = -EBUSY;
 			goto error_unlock;
 		}
